cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or code, please cite the manuscript and this release."
title: "Asymmetry between warmth and clinical substance in multilingual consumer health AI: data and analysis code"
abstract: >-
  Public release of the dataset and reproduction kit accompanying the
  manuscript "Asymmetry between warmth and clinical substance in
  multilingual consumer health AI." Contains 504 chatbot responses
  (21 forum-derived clinical scenarios x 6 languages x 4 widely
  deployed consumer chatbots), 1,008 native-language clinician
  ratings on five Likert dimensions, the paired-English controls
  arm (200 responses with PI ratings), the cross-lingual anchoring
  arm (240 responses with locked-pair LLM-judge scores), the
  remediation stress-test arm, the N=3 reproducibility dataset,
  the LLM-judge cross-validation pilot, framework predictors,
  and a self-contained Python reproduction kit that regenerates
  every reported number and statistical test from the released CSVs.
